Answer:
I would enforce tenant isolation at the data-access layer, retrieval layer, and application authorization boundary. Every stored artifact would carry trusted tenant ownership metadata. The retrieval service would derive tenant identity from authenticated context, never from an LLM-generated filter. I would test adversarial queries that attempt to retrieve another tenant's documents or exploit ambiguous identifiers. I would also isolate caches, logs, embeddings, and evaluation datasets where necessary.
Success criterion: Unauthorized cross-tenant retrieval must be treated as a critical security
