61. How would you design a multi-model LLM gateway?
Answer:
I would build a provider-independent model gateway with standardized request and response contracts. It would support model selection, authentication, quotas, token accounting, retry policies, structured outputs, and telemetry. Model selection could consider task complexity, data classification, latency objectives, context length, cost, and approved provider availability. For example, simple issue classification may use a smaller model, while complex cross-document reasoning may require a stronger model. I would maintain an allowlist of approved models and prevent agents from choosing arbitrary providers.
Trade-off: Provider abstraction improves flexibility, but excessive abstraction can hide
valuable provider-specific capabilities.
62. How would you implement intelligent model
routing?
