I would define routing policies using task type, estimated complexity, quality requirements, data restrictions, and budget. A simple router might use deterministic rules. A more advanced router could use a trained classifier or calibrated model to estimate whether a task needs a larger model. I would benchmark routing against a strong-model baseline. The goal is to reduce cost without materially degrading quality.For example, routine Jira issue categorization might be handled by a smaller model, while architecture analysis uses a larger model.
