66. How would you prevent regressions after changing
an LLM model?
Answer:
I would run the candidate model against the existing evaluation suite before promotion. The suite should include ordinary tasks, complex workflows, safety cases, and known historical failures. I would compare task quality, tool-call behavior, latency, cost, and output-schema compliance. If the model passes offline evaluation, I would deploy it to shadow traffic or a limited canary cohort. I would preserve the previous configuration for rollback.
