68. How would you investigate p99 latency spikes?
Answer:
I would first break down end-to-end latency into queue wait, context preparation, retrieval, model inference, tool execution, and orchestration overhead. I would inspect distributed traces for the slowest requests and correlate them with provider throttling, cold starts, large prompts, or downstream service degradation. For parallel agent workflows, the slowest mandatory dependency often determines completion time. I would compare p50, p95, and p99 distributions rather than optimizing only the average. Possible mitigations include bounded fan-out, caching, smaller prompts, better model routing, concurrency controls, and reducing unnecessary agent steps.
Principal-level insight: Optimize the critical path, not the number of components.
69. How would you define SLOs for an agentic
