correctness of critical actions. Different workload classes may need different SLOs.Interactive question answering may require low latency, while long-running research workflows may prioritize completion reliability. For sensitive operations, unauthorized action rate and audit completeness are important control metrics, though their acceptance criteria should be stricter than ordinary availability targets. I would use error budgets to guide release decisions and reliability investments.
70. How would you optimize LLM cost at platform
scale?
Answer:
I would first establish cost attribution by tenant, agent, workflow, model, and successful business outcome. Then I would optimize unnecessary model calls, oversized prompts, repeated retrieval, and redundant agent delegation. Potential improvements include smaller-model routing, caching where safe, prompt compression, batching when supported, and selective use of reflection. I would set budgets at the workflow and tenant levels. Cost optimization must be evaluated against quality and latency.
Example: Reducing model spend by 30% is not beneficial if the change doubles the rate of
incorrect business actions.
