Topic 2: Context window Sizing
Standard Context Window Cap for Enterprise AI Platforms There is no universal standard context window size for an enterprise AI platform. The context window depends on the underlying LLM, but a production platform should enforce its own limits rather than allowing agents to consume the model's entire available context.
For an enterprise agentic AI platform, I recommend starting with a 32K–64K token operational context budget per agent invocation, even when the underlying model supports 128K, 200K, or more.
Recommended context window sizes
Use case Recommended operational budget
Simple chatbot / FAQ 4K–8K tokens
Tool-calling agent 8K–16K tokens
Enterprise RAG agent 16K–32K tokens
Complex reasoning 32K–64K tokens agent
Multi-agent supervisor 16K–32K tokens
Large document analysis 64K–128K+ tokens
These are engineering starting points, not industry standards or hard model limits. The important distinction is between:
●​ Model context window: Maximum tokens supported by the LLM, including input and generated output where applicable. ●​ Platform context cap: Maximum context your platform allows per invocation to control latency, cost, reliability, and security. ●​ Effective context: The information actually useful for completing the task.
