3. How would you deploy an agentic AI pipeline resiliently?
Interview-ready answer
"I would design resilience at both the infrastructure and workflow-execution layers.
My architecture would use stateless API services, durable queues, horizontally scalable agent workers, persistent workflow state, a model gateway, and a governed MCP tool gateway.
I would deploy services across multiple availability zones and ensure that worker failures do not cause loss of workflow progress.
Every significant workflow transition would be checkpointed in durable storage. Failed tasks would be classified before retrying, and side-effecting operations would use idempotency and reconciliation.
I would also implement circuit breakers, bulkhead isolation, rate limiting, backpressure, and graceful degradation.
Finally, my CI/CD pipeline would include conventional software tests and AI-specific evaluation gates, followed by shadow testing, canary releases, and automated rollback based on reliability, safety, and quality metrics."
