When should an AI platform call an LLM vs. use a deterministic rule engine? For a Principal Engineer designing an enterprise agentic AI platform, this is one of the most important architectural decisions.
The core principle is: Use LLMs for semantic understanding, reasoning, and generation. Use deterministic systems for known rules, authorization, calculations, state transitions, and business-critical execution.
An LLM should not be called merely because a task belongs to an AI application.
