7. What interviewers will challenge you on
At Principal Engineer level, be prepared to go beyond naming AWS services. Interviewers may ask how you handle a worker crash after an external action succeeds but before the checkpoint is saved; how you prevent an old agent version from executing with a revoked policy; how you canary a nondeterministic model; how you prevent a rollout from breaking in-flight workflows; and how you scale when Bedrock quotas are already exhausted.
The best answers connect architecture decisions → failure scenarios → engineering controls → measurable outcomes.
